On Sunday 14 of August 2011 at 23:27:08, Franky Lin wrote:
> On 08/14/2011 11:31 AM, Tomasz Figa wrote:
> > I did some reasearch and it led me to a newer version of the DHD driver,
> > designed for BCM4329 (v. 4.218), which after some modifications (BCD 
protocol
> > version 2, some event IDs, etc.) started to work on my hardware, with one
> > exception: waiting for RxCtrl after sending an "iscanresults" request 
times
> > out. I'm attaching driver debug output at the bottom of this message.
> 
> RxCtrl time out is probably caused by Firmware crash. Based on your 
> description this is the most likely reason. A mismatch between host 
> driver and firmware is not recommended. Is it possible to switch to 
> bcm4329 or get a newer firmware/host driver?
> 

Hi Franky,

Yes, firmware version doesn't match the driver indeed, because I couldn't get 
any newer firmware version than 4.217.95.0 for this chip. As for switching to 
bcm4329, I would like to, but unfortunately it's impossible, because this is 
an already released product and I'm just working on upgrading its software.

Back to the debug log I attached, I also noticed that if a next Tx request is 
started after the waiting RxCtrl, then it manages to continue and receives the 
result correctly (attached log #1). I also looked at some older log without 
added support for BDC version 2 and if it doesn't process the SCAN_COMPLETE 
event but instead ask for iscanresults on programmed timeout, then the request 
completes too (attached log #2).

Anyway, is it possible to obtain a newer firmware for this chip, compatible 
with newer host driver versions?

Best regards,
Tom


